# Every dependency here comes from public npm, whatever the machine's global registry is set to.
#
# This exists because that global default is an Amazon CodeArtifact mirror, and one install picked
# it up: `capacitor-health`'s tarball URL was written into package-lock.json pointing at
# CodeArtifact, which needs a token only that machine has. Vercel's install then failed with
# npm E401 — a build break that reached neither the local builds (the tarball was cached) nor the
# lockfile's other 915 entries. Pinning the registry per-repo means a future install can't repeat it,
# and nobody has to remember `--registry` on the command line.
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
